WEBVTT

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.840
What? Still down seventeen percent?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.780
Please! The connectors used in
this area are from the 20's.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.280
We can't do anything about that!

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.750
The infrastructure in the outlying
areas is supposed to be like that.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.750
The 28th area is better, because
there's a common drain there.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.560
The drains in the 32nd area are
separated by corporation.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.460
An abnormal condition is
confirmed. Shall I fix it?

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.160
Yes, and hurry up.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.530
We have three more places to work on.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.130
I am beginning repair.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.970
I asked the director of the interior areas,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.800
and he said human beings aren't
necessary underground.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.170
I have to go underground in the
middle of the night by myself.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.080
Well, it's a rule, and you'll
have to get over it.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.780
Underground drains from before
the quake need human control.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:31.150
You owe your job to rules like
that. You should appreciate them.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.890
Later.

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.860
Geez! What a big mouth.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.910
Hey, haven't you finished it yet, stupid?

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.630
The K3 parts are broken.
Replacement is necessary.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.030
Oh, great! What luck!

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.770
I didn't bring any old style parts with me!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.280
Damn, everybody passes their
troubles onto other people!

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.150
Screw this, I'm going to have a smoke now!

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.190
Don't scare me!

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.280
Good morning!

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.820
Good morning, Linna!

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.160
Did you hear that Ms. Hatori
in sales got demoted?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.100
No way! Why?

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:26.700
They found out that she's been
giving kick backs to Genom.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.440
I'm shocked. She seemed
like a dedicated woman.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.340
She's a female manager and the
most successful for her age.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.140
It's because of this company.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.450
The people who were born in the
20th century are all thick headed.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:43.020
Oh, the accounting boomer was
looking for you a little while ago.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.490
You made a mistake on your paper work.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.750
Oh, no!

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.620
She was around here a little while ago.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.760
The missing boomer, right?

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.190
What's that?

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:58.470
Haven't you heard? The rumor
about boomers disappearing?

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.270
It's happening in the outlying areas.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.270
Really?

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.140
It's just a rumor.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.240
If it was true, it would be on the news.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.500
Look, the accounting boomer is back.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.050
There are seven cases that are almost certain.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.390
If some suspicious cases are included,

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.020
then the number rises to more
than twenty in six months.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.100
I added apple flavor to the tea.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:40.410
There are no traces of human
beings being attacked.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.100
It means the boomers didn't
transform into mad boomers.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.710
Is someone stealing the boomers?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.510
But then why is news
censorship necessary?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.860
Yes, Sir. It's still being investigated,

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:03.000
but the boomers that disappeared
may have been destroyed on site.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.270
Destroyed? It doesn't seem like
anti-boomer terrorism.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.300
Usually, the only pieces left
at the site are very small,

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.640
so we can't tell exactly
what happened there.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.880
But there is a strong possibility
that the boomers were smashed,

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.150
like they were put in a huge
compactor or something.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.170
Does it have anything to do with
what I've been looking for?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.050
According to the data on your screen,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.690
thirteen out of the fifteen missing
boomers have disappeared

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.230
within a one kilometer radius
in the 28th area,

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:37.000
and all thirteen disappeared while
fifteen meters underground.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.200
The 28th area...

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.800
I checked the area against
the pre-quake map.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:47.140
The lab of a company called
Bioscape was located in the area.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.750
That's all the information up
to the point of the disaster,

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.010
but the thing you've been looking
for might be in this area.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.690
It was a good idea to proceed with
the news censorship, I guess.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:05:59.520
Continue to...

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.120
Just a second!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.330
Someone has hacked into the system!

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.730
I have to cancel your access to
the data temporarily now.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.160
I'll trace and catch the bastard!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.800
Damn! I'm sorry, but I couldn't catch the hacker.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.930
It's okay. Mice are everywhere these days.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.450
That was close!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.920
But I found out that what Sylia
guessed was exactly right.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.660
The boomers listed as missing
concentrate in a certain area.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.180
What concentrates?

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.430
Hey, hey, Nene-chan.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.530
Might you have been using your
PC for private purposes?

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.100
You're going to get in trouble for things like that.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.590
No, I haven't! And don't call me "chan"!

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.280
Our organization isn't a private
company. It's supported by taxes,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.040
so each individual has to have
a proper sense of morality.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:02.440
By the way...

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.250
Well, you were at that club called
Hot Legs, weren't you?

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.990
Uh oh, again!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:14.060
I thought you stayed there
after the show was over.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.660
Do you go there often?

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.800
Not that often.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:21.030
But, Leon-pea, why were you there?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.640
Don't use my name with "pea"!

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:27.340
I thought there was a gloomy
guy standing in the corner,

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.080
and I found out it was you, so I was surprised!

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.280
I went there, because Priss asked me to!

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.580
What?! Priss asked you to come?!

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.020
What's that?

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.890
Priss asked a guy? This is something!

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.190
Is that so?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.820
But, Leon-pea, how long have you known her?

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.060
Well, I don't really know her, you see.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.260
I didn't know that.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.330
She didn't tell me anything!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.000
I see. Priss did ask you.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.660
Nene, are you a good friend of hers?

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:02.910
We're good enough friends to
know each other's e-mail address.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.710
Do you want to know hers?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.750
I didn't intend to ask you
for something like that.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.050
Sorry, I won't tell you.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.320
She told me that she doesn't want
to be followed by weird fans,

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.050
and she'll only tell it to a
few special people.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.420
Especially, men.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.560
Does she have a special man?!

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.660
You want to know her address just
like I thought, don't you?

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.090
I said I didn't intend to ask for it!

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:53.920
But don't you think there's something wrong?

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.060
With what?

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.700
The television news.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.130
There might actually be some boomers missing,

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.170
but what if someone's covering it up?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:06.010
You're still talking about that?

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:09.980
The AD Police live feed was cut in
the middle of an interesting scene.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.080
I feel like they show us only what
they want to show us.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.480
You want to talk about the
Knight Sabers, don't you?

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.820
What information we can or can't
get might be controlled.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:23.450
Are you the kind who connects
everything to a conspiracy?

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:30.060
Hey, you, if we're late
getting back to work,

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.430
the acting section chief will scold us again.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.120
Wait!

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.880
Priss-chan!

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.380
What is it?

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:54.690
Priss, you know Leon who works
at the same station I do, right?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.820
Yeah.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:59.530
He came to your live show, didn't he?

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.290
I didn't know you knew each other.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:04.590
Not really, but what about it?

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:09.700
Well, I realized that you're a girl, Priss.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.570
Do you need to call me about
stupid things like that? Bye!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:15.910
Geez.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.480
Geez, she's not gentle at all!

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:30.120
No way! A man working for the AD Police?

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.930
That's right! I was so surprised.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.930
Like since when, you know?

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:37.230
Isn't that a bad idea?

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:40.430
Why? Leon-chan's a nice guy.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.440
That's not the point!

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:48.440
But he's the late bloomer type.
Priss is like that too, you know.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:53.610
The AD Police are a kind of enemy
of the Knight Sabers, aren't they?

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.850
Is it a good idea for her to hide this?

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:59.650
He's the type who can't go for it
without someone pushing him.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:01.820
Imagine what Sylia would say about them.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:05.660
On top of that, Priss doesn't seem
like she likes the AD Police.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.090
But I wonder why?

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:11.330
I could really enjoy it, if they start
an intimate relationship, so...

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.200
Hey, Nene, are you listening to me?

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.340
One, two, three, four...

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:54.370
Good. Go five meters lower.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:59.010
I don't like working in places
where the ground isn't stable.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:02.380
No matter how hard we work,
nothing built here will be stable.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:06.120
What we're doing now is making
the foundation's sub-foundation.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.780
I wonder how long it'll be before
the start of actual construction?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:16.100
We used to say, don't go underground
in the outlying areas.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.460
What does that mean?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:23.300
Everything below a certain level
was the "Deep Underground".

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.870
There were no records. Those
places were beyond our control.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:31.440
Some companies, and even the
government, built secret facilities.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:38.150
The area where we are now were
crowded by many labs like this.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.550
What do you mean by "secret facilities"?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:46.630
You know, P4 experimentation
and things like that.

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:53.070
When we tunnel around here, we
sometimes hit one of the facilities.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:56.800
If you hit one, don't ever go in.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.410
If you enter one without any preparation,

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:04.410
the ghost of a lab worker who was
buried alive will appear!

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.280
Don't scare me like that, man!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.720
But those rumored places
are around here, right?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.590
Oh, that one?

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.120
What the hell are you talking about?

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.660
You didn't know?

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:19.530
There's a rumor that boomers are
under attack by something.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.160
Well, why don't we let one boomer
go into that right drain?

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.220
Listen. Start measuring the right drain.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.540
Good. Go eighty meters deeper from there.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:55.690
I thought I hated boomers, but

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.560
I might have been scared.

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.700
What is it?

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.640
Nothing.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.670
I see.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:06.710
Sylia, recently, you've been...

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.440
You looked as if you were impatient.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.850
It's time for you to go to bed.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:13.810
Yes, Ma'am.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.020
Wait.

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:21.110
I will protect you.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.980
Hey, what's the matter? What are you doing?

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.230
What? You can't go any farther?

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:00.820
Well, you may come back now.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:15.100
Each algorithm has its own style
that depends on the programmer.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:21.340
And I can identify each algorithm
by reading its style. Look.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:24.280
Incredible, Nene-chan!

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:26.480
I haven't seen a special
technique like this before!

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.820
Call me a genius!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.460
I have a better opinion of you now, Nene-chan.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.860
Excuse me, but I can't ignore
you calling me "chan".

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.230
Would you stop doing that?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.220
Oh, sorry. Then I'll call you Nene.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.700
You should call me Miss Nene!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:47.010
Well, Miss Nene, teach me about this one now.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:49.130
Well, I guess.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:53.780
Nene, I thought you came
here to do some training.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:56.620
Sure, after I finish this.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.180
You can't go straight in this case, so...

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.490
I remember something, Sylia.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:05.590
There's someone who might
be a good partner for Priss.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:09.400
One of my co-workers named
Leon-chan. He's a nice guy.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.400
He seems to be falling in love with Priss.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.900
So I'm thinking of helping him!

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:18.740
Your co-worker? So he's an
AD Police officer, isn't he?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.850
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:30.080
Do you understand what our job is?!

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:31.170
Sylia...

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.290
If you don't know what you've
been doing, you will be fired.

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:36.920
You're nothing but a drag on us.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:46.230
Let's see...

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.850
Excuse me, but I have to leave for a short while.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:01.310
Sure.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.780
You're here early. Did you take a day off?

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:07.920
Yeah. I went somewhere on
business, then came straight here.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.460
What is it?

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:11.890
Nothing. I just came by.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.060
Did I interfere with your work?

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:14.530
No.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.330
Say, Priss...

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.970
Can I ask you something?

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.470
About what?

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:25.990
The AD Police.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.780
I've been wondering why you
hate them so much.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.580
Did Nene tell you something?

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:35.510
No, not at all. I haven't heard anything from her.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:36.820
She's good.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.750
She did something she shouldn't have!

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:42.090
No, I'm the one wondering about it.

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:44.890
I just don't like their way of doing things.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.730
When they have a mission as a pretext,

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.660
they don't care how horribly they hurt people.

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:54.430
I can't stand a grandstanding attitude like that.

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:55.800
Is that all?

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.800
Priss! Linna! A mad boomer has appeared.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:12.550
How long do you intend to pout?! Let's go!

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.360
What's wrong, Nene?

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:24.190
Priss, Linna, hurry up and change!

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.260
Leave her alone.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.700
I can do it! I can do it!

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.910
Run!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.360
We did it! We got here first!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.590
Unusual, isn't it?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.730
What the hell is that?!

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.670
We don't have time to be impressed!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.750
I wonder if we'll be able to control
it until the tank gets here?

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.240
I guess that's impossible.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.840
Geez! The same pattern as always.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.300
Linna, wait until you're close enough!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:44.580
This is the place. The 28th area.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.070
Linna, behind you!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.080
It's mine!

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:02.430
That idiot did it again!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:04.700
Nene, don't attack it from the front!

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:05.760
I...

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:10.230
I'm not a drag on you!

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.800
I did it!

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.150
I told you!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.470
Nene!

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.980
What?!

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.530
What the hell?!

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.470
What the hell is that?!

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:58.570
Next Episode

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:02.490
Hey, hey, hey! Guess what?!

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:05.790
Leon-chan was removed from the
investigation of that huge thing!

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:09.500
Some kind of pressure was applied
to him I guess, but it's strange!

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:12.040
It seems as if Genom is working
in the shadows.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.000
I can sense the strong
smell of conspiracy.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.590
First of all, where did that thing come from?

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:19.760
Could it possibly be a crime syndicate?

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:21.720
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
